    "summary": "Children\u2019s nightwear comes in all kinds of fun patterns and cozy fabrics; however, if they catch fire, it can lead to serious burns. \n \nIf you are a business that sells children\u2019s nightwear, you must comply with certain safety standards in New Zealand. The Commerce Commission is responsible for enforcement of these safety standards.\n \nLearn more: \nhttps://www.comcom.govt.nz/business/your-obligations-as-a-business/product-safety-standards/childrens-nightwear/",
